# Changelog

## Unreleased

### Graphical application and macOS workflow

- Added a native PySide6 project-generation GUI.
- Added Source WAV, XPJ template, musical layout, root, scale, pad-bank, project-name, and destination controls.
- Reused the validated `BankSpec` and project-package generation pipeline from the graphical workflow.
- Added GUI working, success, and error states.
- Added remembered browse locations and reveal-in-Finder support.
- Refined the GUI into separate Musical Setup and Pad Bank sections.
- Added PyInstaller-based macOS application packaging and a package-aware GUI launcher.
- Validated the Finder-launched `.app` generation workflow on physical MPC Sample hardware.
- Automated test suite reached 146 passing tests at the latest validated development checkpoint.

### User-facing project generation

- Added the `mpctk` command-line entry point and `mpctk generate` workflow.
- Added complete project-package generation from a source WAV, structural XPJ template, `BankSpec`, destination, and project name.
- Added automatic ProjectData directory creation and source-WAV copying.
- Added MPC Bank A-H / Pad 1-16 addressing and automatic source-sample discovery.
- Added WAV sample injection into project and track sample pools.
- Validated generated packages on physical MPC Sample hardware.

### Musical generation

- Added chromatic bank generation.
- Added major and natural minor Scale Pad generation.
- Added musical root parsing, enharmonic note support, and source-to-target root transposition.
- Added `BankSpec` as the high-level musical bank specification.
- Added Chromatic Keyboard and Scale Pads layout concepts.
- Added verified MPC coarse-tuning range enforcement.

### XPJ foundation

- Added gzip-compressed XPJ reading and writing.
- Added structured project, track, instrument, layer, sample-reference, and slice models.
- Added preservation of unknown XPJ fields through `raw_data`.
- Added layer coarse-tune editing and cloning.
- Validated written and edited XPJ projects on physical MPC Sample hardware.

## v0.1.0-alpha

- Initial repository structure.
